# Structure Rules

## Project layout

```
<project>/
├── .cursor/
│   ├── rules/                 # Always-on REA investigation rules
│   ├── skills/                # /setup-investigation, /start-investigation, update-docs
│   └── agents/worker.md       # Cheap executor for mechanical steps
├── AGENTS.md                  # Pointer for non-Cursor agents
├── docs/                      # How to start, authorization, clone instructions
├── investigations/            # One folder per target
│   └── <slug>/
│       ├── TARGET.md          # What, where, authorization
│       ├── QUESTIONS.md       # Checklist of questions and evidence needed
│       ├── EVIDENCE.md        # Evidence IDs, limitations, unknowns
│       ├── FINDINGS.md        # Plain-language answers
│       └── NOTES.md           # Working notes
├── targets/                   # Authorized artifacts (gitignored binaries)
├── evidence/                  # Exported REA bundles + raw captures
│   └── raw/                   # HAR, pcap, dumps — gitignored
├── reconstructions/           # Our own implementations of understood features
└── notes/                     # Scratch, not a formal investigation
```

## File placement rules

- New investigations go in `investigations/<slug>/` using the files in `investigations/_template/`.
- Authorized binaries and app trees go in `targets/` (or stay at an existing absolute install path). Do not commit them.
- Exported REA bundles go in `evidence/`. Raw captures go in `evidence/raw/`.
- Companion code we write goes in `reconstructions/<feature>/`.
- Agent/reference docs go in `docs/` — see `documentation.mdc`.
- Cursor rules live in `.cursor/rules/` as `.mdc` files. Never create a rule with a `.md` extension.
- Cursor skills live in `.cursor/skills/<skill-name>/SKILL.md`.
- `AGENTS.md` is a thin pointer. Don't duplicate rule content into it.

## Naming conventions

- Investigation slugs: kebab-case (`notes-search`, `dx-ball-pan`).
- Notes: `TARGET.md`, `QUESTIONS.md`, `EVIDENCE.md`, `FINDINGS.md`, `NOTES.md`.
- Reconstructions: kebab-case directories, stack-native file names inside.

## When creating new files

1. Check whether an existing investigation folder already covers this target.
2. Never create a file outside this layout without asking first.
3. If a new top-level directory is needed, propose it and explain why.
